changes.change:
The description («Где что лежит») now states the tie behaviour exactly. With k forged lines at time F followed by m real lines dated before F − 120 s, every forged line conflicts with every such real line:
- while m ≤ k, the real lines are marked and the forged ones count, and one forged line is enough;
- from m = k+1, the forged lines are marked;
- real lines dated F − 120 s or later never conflict, so with no further real lines in that window the wrong mark is permanent.
AC4 (б) now says a marked line drops out of the conflicts. AC13 adds this to the README «### Ограничения» and to its grep list («одной вписанной строки», «навсегда»).
